<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  The one process in this mod whose numbers had to change, and not because of the framework.

  Daemon976 wrote it with usesQuality and a seven-step qualityDays, because in the 1.4 Sushi
  add-on VCE_SoySauce carried a CompQuality and a CompProperties_StackByQuality. In 1.6 both are
  gone from the def: soy sauce is a plain condiment with no quality at all. Asking the framework
  to set a quality on a thing that has no CompQuality is asking for a null reference at the moment
  the batch finishes.

  So quality is out and the process is a flat wait instead. Ten days is the Sushi add-on's own
  1.6 figure - its VCE_SoybeansToSauce runs 600,000 ticks - rather than the one to sixty days the
  quality ladder used to span. capacityFactor is Daemon976's, untouched.

  The original mod added this def by PatchOperationAdd on /Defs from inside a
  PatchOperationFindMod. It is a plain def in a folder gated by packageId now.
-->
<Defs>

  <ProcessorFramework.ProcessDef>
    <defName>PF_VCE_SoySauce</defName>
    <thingDef>VCE_SoySauce</thingDef>
    <ingredientFilter>
      <thingDefs>
        <li>VCE_RawSoybean</li>
      </thingDefs>
    </ingredientFilter>
    <capacityFactor>2.5</capacityFactor>
    <processDays>10</processDays>
  </ProcessorFramework.ProcessDef>

</Defs>
